{
  "abstract": "Let $C$ be the Collatz map, $C(x)=x/2$ for even $x$ and $C(x)=(3x+1)/2$ for odd $x$, and let $\\phi_n(x)=(-1)^{C^n(x)}$ on $\\mathbb Z/2^{n+1}\\mathbb Z$. Fix an odd $c$ with $3\\nmid c$ and $K>0$. We prove that, uniformly in $|k-n/2|\\le K\\sqrt n$,\n$$\\widehat{\\phi}_n(c\\,3^k)=\\bigl(G_c+o(1)\\bigr)\\,2^{-n}\\tbinom nk ,\\qquad G_c=\\sum_{d\\in\\mathbb Z}C_d(c).$$\nThe constants $C_d(c)$ are expectations of characters of the joint real and $3$-adic boundary of the affine Collatz recursion, and the series converges absolutely. For $d>0$ the needed decay comes from Tao's $3$-adic estimate. For $d<0$ we prove $|\\mathbb E\\,e(c3^mR/2)|\\ll_A m^{-A}$ (odd $c\\ge1$) for the perpetuity $R=\\sum_{i\\ge1}3^{i-1}2^{-a_1-\\cdots-a_i}$ with iid geometric gaps, by a stopped version of Tao's renewal argument. In the tail estimates the count-slice weight is measurable with respect to Tao's pairing of gaps, so the weighted conditioning bound of rStation collatz Paper 54, Corollary 4, applies; our input is this specific weight, its boundedness and its use with the real-side estimate. We give no rate, we do not prove $G_c\\ne0$, and the constants are not uniform in $c$.",
